<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Total-conversion behavior, CONFIGURATION-DATABASE half.

  This file may only ever touch Configuration-database tables (Players,
  PlayerItems, ...). It is wired to FrontEndActions ONLY in Warmstone.modinfo.
  Its Gameplay-database counterpart is Warmstone_HideVanillaLeaders_Gameplay.xml.
  Keeping them separate is not cosmetic - see REVISION 3 below.

  REVISION 3 (this file). Revisions 1 and 2 both failed, and the reason was
  finally found in the *live* log at
  %LOCALAPPDATA%\Firaxis Games\Sid Meier's Civilization VI\Logs\Database.log:

      [Configuration] ERROR: no such table: CivilizationLeaders
      [Configuration]: In Query - DELETE FROM CivilizationLeaders;
      [Configuration] ERROR: ... error executing the delete statement!

  The old single Warmstone_HideVanillaLeaders.xml mixed `Players` (a
  Configuration-database table) and `CivilizationLeaders` (a Gameplay-database
  table) in one file, and the .modinfo loaded that one file into BOTH databases.
  In the Configuration pass `CivilizationLeaders` does not exist, so the file
  aborted ("ModdingUpdateConfigurationDatabase - Error Loading XML" in
  Modding.log) and the `Players` delete in the same file never committed. That is
  why every vanilla leader was still in the picker. The abort also skipped every
  remaining Warmstone frontend action, which is why Stalwarts_Config.xml was
  never loaded at all and the Stalwart leader never appeared.

  Two other things revisions 1-2 got wrong, both fixed here:

  1. Domain. The picker does not read `Players` wholesale - it reads the domain
     bound to the `PlayerLeader` setup parameter for the active ruleset, per
     Configuration/Data/Schema/AdditionalTables.sql (`Domain` DEFAULT
     'Players:StandardPlayers') and the RulesetDomainOverrides rows in
     DLC/Expansion*/Config/Expansion*_Players.xml:
         RULESET_EXPANSION_2 / PlayerLeader -> Players:Expansion2_Players
     So a Gathering Storm game reads only Players:Expansion2_Players. A row with
     no Domain lands in Players:StandardPlayers and is invisible there. Every
     re-added row below is therefore declared once per domain, exactly the way
     DLC/Australia/Data/Australia_Config.xml does it.

  2. Load order. The bare <Delete/> removes every row present *at the time it
     runs*. Modding.log showed the old LoadOrder of -10 running this at
     t=2782016.120, while DLC/Expansion2/Config/Expansion2_Players.xml loaded
     afterwards at t=2782017.079 and repopulated the table. The frontend action
     for this file now carries a LoadOrder of 100 so it runs after all DLC
     config, and Stalwarts_Config.xml runs later still at 110.

  Kept: CIVILIZATION_ROME / LEADER_TRAJAN, so AI opponents have at least one
  non-Warmstone option while only Stalwarts exists on the Warmstone side. The
  re-added rows reuse Rome/Trajan's own shipped Firaxis LOC keys and icons
  verbatim (taken from Base/Assets/Configuration/Data/Players.xml) - that is
  re-pointing at already-shipped vanilla content, not new authored copy.

  PlayerItems is deliberately left alone: rows belonging to civs that are no
  longer in the picker are simply never queried, and deleting the table would
  also throw away Rome's own unique-item entries for no benefit.

  This only ever affects games created while this mod is enabled - Civ6 rebuilds
  the configuration database from currently-active content each time mod state
  changes.
-->
<GameInfo>
	<Players>
		<Delete/>
		<Row Domain="Players:StandardPlayers" CivilizationType="CIVILIZATION_ROME" LeaderType="LEADER_TRAJAN" CivilizationName="LOC_CIVILIZATION_ROME_NAME" CivilizationIcon="ICON_CIVILIZATION_ROME" LeaderName="LOC_LEADER_TRAJAN_NAME" LeaderIcon="ICON_LEADER_TRAJAN" CivilizationAbilityName="LOC_TRAIT_CIVILIZATION_ALL_ROADS_TO_ROME_NAME" CivilizationAbilityDescription="LOC_TRAIT_CIVILIZATION_ALL_ROADS_TO_ROME_DESCRIPTION" CivilizationAbilityIcon="ICON_CIVILIZATION_ROME" LeaderAbilityName="LOC_TRAIT_LEADER_TRAJANS_COLUMN_NAME" LeaderAbilityDescription="LOC_TRAIT_LEADER_TRAJANS_COLUMN_DESCRIPTION" LeaderAbilityIcon="ICON_LEADER_TRAJAN"/>
		<Row Domain="Players:Expansion1_Players" CivilizationType="CIVILIZATION_ROME" LeaderType="LEADER_TRAJAN" CivilizationName="LOC_CIVILIZATION_ROME_NAME" CivilizationIcon="ICON_CIVILIZATION_ROME" LeaderName="LOC_LEADER_TRAJAN_NAME" LeaderIcon="ICON_LEADER_TRAJAN" CivilizationAbilityName="LOC_TRAIT_CIVILIZATION_ALL_ROADS_TO_ROME_NAME" CivilizationAbilityDescription="LOC_TRAIT_CIVILIZATION_ALL_ROADS_TO_ROME_DESCRIPTION" CivilizationAbilityIcon="ICON_CIVILIZATION_ROME" LeaderAbilityName="LOC_TRAIT_LEADER_TRAJANS_COLUMN_NAME" LeaderAbilityDescription="LOC_TRAIT_LEADER_TRAJANS_COLUMN_DESCRIPTION" LeaderAbilityIcon="ICON_LEADER_TRAJAN"/>
		<Row Domain="Players:Expansion2_Players" CivilizationType="CIVILIZATION_ROME" LeaderType="LEADER_TRAJAN" CivilizationName="LOC_CIVILIZATION_ROME_NAME" CivilizationIcon="ICON_CIVILIZATION_ROME" LeaderName="LOC_LEADER_TRAJAN_NAME" LeaderIcon="ICON_LEADER_TRAJAN" CivilizationAbilityName="LOC_TRAIT_CIVILIZATION_ALL_ROADS_TO_ROME_NAME" CivilizationAbilityDescription="LOC_TRAIT_CIVILIZATION_ALL_ROADS_TO_ROME_DESCRIPTION" CivilizationAbilityIcon="ICON_CIVILIZATION_ROME" LeaderAbilityName="LOC_TRAIT_LEADER_TRAJANS_COLUMN_NAME" LeaderAbilityDescription="LOC_TRAIT_LEADER_TRAJANS_COLUMN_DESCRIPTION" LeaderAbilityIcon="ICON_LEADER_TRAJAN"/>
	</Players>
</GameInfo>
